1
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:12,360
Lena buys a book for 7 dollars 85, and a pen for 2 dollars 40.

2
00:00:12,410 --> 00:00:15,460
She pays with a 20 dollar note.

3
00:00:15,510 --> 00:00:17,590
How much change should she get?

4
00:00:17,640 --> 00:00:21,180
Pause the video and work it out.

5
00:00:21,230 --> 00:00:23,390
First add the prices.

6
00:00:23,440 --> 00:00:26,460
7.85 plus 2.40 is 10.25.

7
00:00:26,510 --> 00:00:29,270
Then take that away from 20.

8
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:31,580
20 minus 10.25 is 9.75.

9
00:00:31,630 --> 00:00:35,150
Lena gets 9 dollars 75 change.

10
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:37,180
Remember column addition.

11
00:00:37,230 --> 00:00:40,840
Line up ones under ones, and tens under tens.

12
00:00:40,890 --> 00:00:42,360
476 plus 58.

13
00:00:42,410 --> 00:00:45,780
Carry when a column adds up to 10 or more.

14
00:00:45,830 --> 00:00:47,800
The answer is 534.

15
00:00:47,850 --> 00:00:51,480
With decimals, the rule is: line up the decimal points.

16
00:00:51,530 --> 00:00:56,170
Then every digit sits under a digit with the same place value.

17
00:00:56,220 --> 00:00:57,700
7.85 plus 2.4.

18
00:00:57,750 --> 00:01:02,610
Write 2.4 as 2.40, so there are no gaps.

19
00:01:02,660 --> 00:01:04,400
Add from the right.

20
00:01:04,450 --> 00:01:05,720
5 plus 0 is 5.

21
00:01:05,770 --> 00:01:08,840
8 plus 4 is 12: write 2, carry 1.

22
00:01:08,890 --> 00:01:11,460
7 plus 2 plus 1 is 10.

23
00:01:11,510 --> 00:01:16,820
The decimal point in the answer goes straight under the other points.

24
00:01:16,870 --> 00:01:18,840
The total is 10.25.

25
00:01:18,890 --> 00:01:19,670
Your turn.

26
00:01:19,720 --> 00:01:21,570
Work out 0.9 plus 0.35.

27
00:01:21,620 --> 00:01:25,200
Pause the video and try it.

28
00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:27,120
Write 0.9 as 0.90.

29
00:01:27,170 --> 00:01:32,560
90 hundredths plus 35 hundredths is 125 hundredths.

30
00:01:32,610 --> 00:01:35,130
The answer is 1.25.

31
00:01:35,180 --> 00:01:38,610
Subtracting works the same way.

32
00:01:38,660 --> 00:01:40,290
20 minus 10.25.

33
00:01:40,340 --> 00:01:42,860
Write 20 as 20.00.

34
00:01:42,910 --> 00:01:48,160
Subtract column by column from the right, exchanging when you need to.

35
00:01:48,210 --> 00:01:50,140
The answer is 9.75.

36
00:01:50,190 --> 00:01:52,480
Check by adding back.

37
00:01:52,530 --> 00:01:55,470
9.75 plus 10.25 is 20.

38
00:01:55,520 --> 00:01:59,370
With negative numbers, use the integer rules.

39
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:04,500
4.2 minus negative 1.3 is 4.2 plus 1.3, which is 5.5.

40
00:02:04,550 --> 00:02:05,890
Here is the method.

41
00:02:05,940 --> 00:02:09,080
Step 1: estimate first, by rounding.

42
00:02:09,130 --> 00:02:15,810
Step 2: write the numbers with the decimal points lined up, and fill the gaps with zeros.

43
00:02:15,860 --> 00:02:20,400
Step 3: add or subtract column by column, from the right.

44
00:02:20,450 --> 00:02:24,780
Step 4: put the decimal point in the answer, under the others.

45
00:02:24,830 --> 00:02:27,580
Then compare with your estimate.

46
00:02:27,630 --> 00:02:31,040
Work out 4.7 plus 0.36 plus 12.05.

47
00:02:31,090 --> 00:02:36,170
First estimate: 5 plus 0 plus 12 is about 17.

48
00:02:36,220 --> 00:02:38,100
Line up the points.

49
00:02:38,150 --> 00:02:41,350
Hundredths: 0 plus 6 plus 5 is 11.

50
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:42,970
Write 1, carry 1.

51
00:02:43,020 --> 00:02:46,500
Tenths: 7 plus 3 plus 0 plus 1 is 11.

52
00:02:46,550 --> 00:02:48,130
Write 1, carry 1.

53
00:02:48,180 --> 00:02:50,590
The answer is 17.11.

54
00:02:50,640 --> 00:02:52,780
Work out 8 minus 2.374.

55
00:02:52,830 --> 00:02:56,180
Write 8 with 3 decimal places.

56
00:02:56,230 --> 00:03:02,660
Exchange: 8 ones become 7 ones, 9 tenths, 9 hundredths and 10 thousandths.

57
00:03:02,710 --> 00:03:03,880
Now subtract.

58
00:03:03,930 --> 00:03:06,300
The answer is 5.626.

59
00:03:06,350 --> 00:03:07,100
Your turn.

60
00:03:07,150 --> 00:03:09,680
Work out 2.5 minus negative 0.7.

61
00:03:09,730 --> 00:03:12,860
Pause and work it out.

62
00:03:12,910 --> 00:03:16,710
Subtracting a negative is the same as adding.

63
00:03:16,760 --> 00:03:18,980
2.5 plus 0.7 is 3.2.

64
00:03:19,030 --> 00:03:21,980
A recipe needs 0.75 kilograms of flour.

65
00:03:22,030 --> 00:03:23,680
Ama has 2.1 kilograms.

66
00:03:23,730 --> 00:03:25,760
She makes the recipe twice.

67
00:03:25,810 --> 00:03:28,080
How much flour is left?

68
00:03:28,130 --> 00:03:33,400
She uses 0.75 plus 0.75, which is 1.5 kilograms.

69
00:03:33,450 --> 00:03:35,590
2.10 minus 1.50 is 0.6.

70
00:03:35,640 --> 00:03:38,710
She has 0.6 kilograms left.

71
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:41,630
Raj works out 3.6 plus 1.25 like this.

72
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:44,400
He lined up the digits on the right.

73
00:03:44,450 --> 00:03:46,180
What went wrong?

74
00:03:46,230 --> 00:03:49,080
The 6 tenths were added to 5 hundredths.

75
00:03:49,130 --> 00:03:52,330
The decimal points are not in a line.

76
00:03:52,380 --> 00:03:56,090
Line up the points and fill in a zero.

77
00:03:56,140 --> 00:03:58,920
3.60 plus 1.25 is 4.85.

78
00:03:58,970 --> 00:04:02,240
Doctors add and subtract decimals every day.

79
00:04:02,290 --> 00:04:06,720
Normal body temperature is about 37 degrees Celsius.

80
00:04:06,770 --> 00:04:09,940
Suppose a thermometer reads 38.6 degrees.

81
00:04:09,990 --> 00:04:12,770
How far above normal is that?

82
00:04:12,820 --> 00:04:14,750
38.6 minus 37.0 is 1.6.

83
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:18,530
The temperature is 1.6 degrees above normal.

84
00:04:18,580 --> 00:04:20,460
That is a fever.

85
00:04:20,510 --> 00:04:21,940
One last question.

86
00:04:21,990 --> 00:04:23,760
What is 10 minus 0.01?

87
00:04:23,810 --> 00:04:27,390
Pause the video and answer.

88
00:04:27,440 --> 00:04:29,370
Write 10 as 10.00.

89
00:04:29,420 --> 00:04:31,790
Take away 1 hundredth.

90
00:04:31,840 --> 00:04:34,430
The answer is 9.99.

91
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:39,450
To remember: line up the decimal points, and fill gaps with zeros.

92
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:43,050
Add or subtract as you do with whole numbers.

93
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:46,590
Use the integer rules for negative decimals.

94
00:04:46,640 --> 00:04:50,830
Estimate first, and check with the inverse operation.

95
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:56,030
Great work! Now practise lesson 4.2 on Camday.
